DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T120000
SUMMARY:The Integration Blueprint: Choosing the Right Path in Microsoft Fa
 bric
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn a world of multiple tools and en
 dless data sources\, how do you design the right integration strategy in M
 icrosoft Fabric?\n\nJoin us for a live demo-driven session that breaks dow
 n the real-world patterns\, use cases\, and best practices for landing\, t
 ransforming\, and orchestrating data in Microsoft Fabric.\n\nWhether you'r
 e working with a Lakehouse\, Data Warehouse\, Eventhouse\, or SQL Database
 \, this session gives you the playbook to select and combine the right too
 ls for the job.\n\nWe'll walk through:\n\n* Landing data using Data Pipeli
 nes\, OneLake shortcuts\, and external connections\n* Transforming and cle
 aning data using Notebooks (Spark) for scale and flexibility\n* Business l
 ogic and last-mile transformation using Dataflows Gen2\n* How to orchestra
 te it all using Fabric Data Pipelines for repeatable\, maintainable workfl
 ows\n* When and why to land your data into Lakehouses\, Data Warehouses\, 
 Eventhouses\, or SQL endpoints\n\nYou'll walk away with:\n\n* A clear unde
 rstanding of which tools to use when across the Fabric integration stack\n
 * A working knowledge of how to combine multiple integration techniques in
  one solution\n* Architecture patterns and decision criteria for building 
 scalable data landing zones\n\nLive demos you can replicate to accelerate 
 your own Fabric journey\n\nThis session is a part of a series - learn more
  **[here](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1621/?wt.mc_id=
 meetup_S-1621_webpage_reactor)**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3139
 45187/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260325T172005Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T172005Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
