X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_313946136@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260429T035616Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T110000
SUMMARY:OpenClawNet - Automation + Azure + Foundry
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn this session we will make the ag
 ent production-ready. We will add job scheduling as a background service\,
  integrate Azure OpenAI and Azure AI Foundry as cloud model providers\, bu
 ild monitoring dashboards\, and write unit tests that verify the entire st
 ack.\n\nAt the end we will have a complete\, tested\, cloud-ready agent pl
 atform with production-grade error handling\, multiple AI model providers\
 , scheduled automation\, and observability dashboards. Deploy it to Azure 
 Container Apps\, App Service\, or run it on-premises with Ollama.\n\n**Key
  Topics & Technologies:**\n\n* BackgroundService for long-running jobs\n* 
 Azure OpenAI integration and model selection\n* Azure AI Foundry (inferenc
 e\, deployments\, evaluation)\n* Unit testing patterns for agents and tool
 s\n* Health checks and system diagnostics\n* Job queuing and status tracki
 ng\n* Configuration for multi-environment deployments (local\, staging\, p
 roduction)\n\nPre-requisites:\n\n* **Experience:** Intermediate C# and ASP
 .NET Core knowledge (not a .NET 101)\n* **Environment:** .NET 10 SDK\, VS 
 Code + GitHub Copilot (or Visual Studio)\, Docker (for Ollama)\n* **Option
 al:** Azure subscription (for Sessions 3–4\, but local development works
  fine throughout)\n* **Mindset:** Curiosity about AI agents\, willingness 
 to follow along live and ask questions
